+**Explore phase**:
+The agent phase that writes a **Task set**'s **Exploration report**. A fresh Explorer is handed the set's manifest listing, its task bodies and its spec; its runs are filed as **Captured run**s of phase `explore` and spend against a retry cap of their own. In a **Drain** it runs at the head of the loop, before any task is selected, only for a set that declared the **Explore directive**, has AFK work to build and has no report; `[work.explore].enabled` gates it machine-wide and defaults on — safe because the set's own declaration is the trigger. It declines for a **Human completion**. It is the one agent phase that gates: a pass that gives up parks the set as an **Explore-failed Task set**. `pop tasks explore <set>` runs it by hand on any set, whatever the directive says, and rewrites an existing report.
